          "title": "You'll want to know: сковорода",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "сковорода (skovorodá) — \"a frying pan\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "сковорода (skovorodá) from Proto-Slavic skovorda — inherited, with Church Slavonic сковрада. Vasmer calls its further origin unclear; a comparison with Old High German scart-îsan, \"a frying pan\", has been made, and Szemerényi derived it from an Iranian word for \"bowl\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
